The forward lens's count (line 7 of 1.0) refers to schema 1.0's count through
the lineage rather than to input, found by checkReferences at bind. A lens may
refer only to input, its own body and CUE's builtin packages.

The position is the referring result field, looked up in the lens value by
the finding's path, so the error lands on the author's line. The reference
itself is read from the lens's syntax, which has no positions.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
schema: {
	title: string
	count?: int
}
-- ship/1.0.thema --
schema: {
	title: string
	count: int & <10
}

forward: {
	count: to.schema.count
}

backward: {
	count: to.count
}
-- out/error --
lens 0.0->1.0: result.count refers to schemas["1"]["0"].schema.count, a schema; a lens may refer only to input, its own body and CUE's builtin packages (rule ref-lens-to-schema):
    ship/1.0.thema:7:9
-- out/positions --
lens 0.0->1.0: result.count refers to schemas["1"]["0"].schema.count, a schema; a lens may refer only to input, its own body and CUE's builtin packages (rule ref-lens-to-schema)
	authored ship/1.0.thema:7:9
